# Want to see the app running RIGHT NOW with zero setup below? Uncomment this
# one line and skip everything else in this file for today:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_BYPASS_AUTH=true
#
# It replaces the login screen with a "pick a role" preview so you can click
# through the Owner/Manager/Tenant dashboards with no Supabase project at
# all. Nothing about real auth changes — it's dev-only, clearly banner'd in
# the UI, and everything below still applies once you're ready to wire up
# real accounts (see src/lib/dev-bypass.ts to remove it later).

# Supabase — create a project at https://supabase.com, then Project Settings > API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Phone OTP auth needs a way to actually send the code:
#  - Cheapest for now: Authentication > Providers > Phone > "Test OTPs" —
#    add a line like +919999999999=123456 and sign in with that exact
#    number + code, no SMS provider account needed at all. Dev-only.
#  - For real users: configure a real SMS provider (MSG91 or Twilio) in the
#    same Phone provider settings — this is a real per-SMS cost once live.
# No key needed here either way — both are configured inside the dashboard.

# --- Added in later phases, not needed for Phase 0 ---
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# WHATSAPP_BSP_API_KEY=       # e.g. AiSensy / Gupshup, added in Phase 4
